1
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:12,166
Every how-to video plays at the same speed, whether you keep up, or not.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,606
Falls are the second-leading cause of unintentional injury death worldwide.

3
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:27,377
In one survey, three in four people didn't finish their home physical therapy exercises.

4
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:32,198
And most cardiac arrests outside hospital happen at home,

5
00:00:32,198 --> 00:00:34,864
where nobody is checking your form.

6
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:40,836
At least nine in ten deaf children are born to hearing parents.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,050
And a video can't see whether your hands are right.

8
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,408
InStep is the video that waits for you.

9
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:58,667
Prop up your phone. It becomes the camera: an external camera, not the TV.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,620
Pose tracking runs in the phone's browser. Only body points travel to the TV,

11
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:06,802
never video.

12
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,781
At each key moment, the lesson pauses,

13
00:01:11,781 --> 00:01:15,078
and continues only when your pose is right.

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,093
It counts your reps, times your balance, and if you're stuck,

15
00:01:21,093 --> 00:01:23,524
a coach gives one short, kind tip.

16
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:33,682
Safety comes first: no balance work until a chair is beside you.

17
00:01:33,682 --> 00:01:37,167
And if the camera drops, the lesson stops.

18
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:46,129
The same engine teaches sign-language hand shapes, hand rehab, and CPR rhythm:

19
00:01:46,129 --> 00:01:49,126
practice only, not certification.

20
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:54,815
Kids act out a story. And two people can practise together.

21
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:02,909
A physiotherapist or teacher records a lesson once, on a phone.

22
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:09,808
InStep finds the still moments, suggests the steps, and publishes it to the TV.

23
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:16,007
Under the hood: an open lesson format called .istep,

24
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:22,355
one pure TypeScript gate engine, shared by the phone, the server and the TV,

25
00:02:22,700 --> 00:02:26,430
and an open-source Vega player that any app can use.

26
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:34,430
InStep. The video that waits for you.

